\section{Causal Profiling: Concept and Implementation}\label{sec:causal-concept}

\subsection{The Causal Profiling Idea}\label{sec:causal-idea}

Causal profiling~\cite{curtsinger2013codepet} measures the \emph{causal effect}
of optimizing a specific code location.  The key insight is that the effect of
\emph{speeding up} code at location $l$ by factor $s$ is equivalent to
\emph{slowing down} all other code by a compensating factor.

\begin{definition}[Virtual Speedup]\label{def:virtual-speedup}
A \emph{virtual speedup} of $s\%$ at location $l$ is achieved by inserting
delays in all code \emph{except} at $l$, such that the program's total execution
time increases by the amount that would be saved by speeding up $l$ by $s\%$.
\end{definition}

