\section{Integration with Compiler Optimization}\label{sec:causal-integration}

\subsection{Profile-Guided Optimization with Causal Profiles}\label{sec:causal-pgo}

Causal profiles can guide compiler optimization decisions:

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Inlining decisions:} Prioritize inlining functions with steep
      causal profiles (high optimization potential).
\item \textbf{Loop optimization:} Prioritize optimizing loops with steep causal
      profiles.
\item \textbf{Code layout:} Place code with high causal impact in hot code
      regions.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Feedback-Directed Causal Profiling}\label{sec:causal-feedback}

An iterative approach combines causal profiling with optimization:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Run causal profiling to identify the best optimization target.
\item Apply the optimization.
\item Re-run causal profiling on the optimized program.
\item Repeat until no significant optimization opportunities remain.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Automated Optimization Selection}\label{sec:causal-auto}

In principle, causal profiling can be used to automatically select
optimizations:
\begin{enumerate}
\item For each available optimization, estimate its virtual speedup at the
      affected code locations.
\item Use the causal profile to predict the program speedup.
\item Apply the optimization with the highest predicted benefit.
\end{enumerate}

This approach requires a cost model that maps optimizations to virtual speedups,
which is challenging but feasible for certain classes of optimizations (e.g.,
vectorization, where the speedup can be estimated from the instruction mix).

\begin{insight}
Causal profiling shifts the focus of performance analysis from \emph{observation}
(where does the program spend time?) to \emph{intervention} (what happens if I
change this?).  This causal perspective is more aligned with the goals of
optimization: we do not just want to know where time is spent; we want to know
where time \emph{can be saved}.  The connection to causal inference in
statistics and the potential for integrating causal profiling with machine
learning-based optimization are exciting directions for future research.
\end{insight}

